From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tyn <tyn@localhost>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:11:22 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] tyn: sg-pc HELP screen from the original Game.exe
 (HelpMenuType.SGHD)

The STEINS;GATE (Steam) HELP screen as the original draws and handles it, instead of the 0023 fallback that left
HELP at once. Layout, art and behaviour come from the original Game.exe: the draw routine 0x4351f0, the input routine
0x435640, Help(Init) 0x4355a0 and the hit areas at 0x52b670. The pages are the full screen pictures of manual.mpk, so
translated data shows its own pages.

- New generic class UI::SGHD::HelpMenu + Profile::SGHD::HelpMenu (HelpMenuType.SGHD): pages, page number, tabs and
  button guide are profile data.
- Behaviour as the original: drawn while the script's submenu is HELP (SW_SYSSUBMENUNO 11) with the opacity
  SW_SYSSUBMENUCT / 32 * SW_SYSSUBMENUALPHA / 256, the page coming in from x = -400 while the counter runs; it starts
  at the first page every time; next / previous page (R1 / L1 = E / Q, mouse wheel) and the tabs slide the new page in
  over the old one (16 frames, 48 px per frame, fading in; next page and tabs from the left, previous page from the
  right), no input while it slides; the hovered tab, else the current page's tab, blinks; Back raises SF_SUBMENUEXIT
  and SF_MANUALLOAD_END (ends the script's manual loading thread). The pages are preloaded (InstHelp(Init) already
  reports the manual as loaded).
- The original writes the controller page's button names over PAGE2 only when its launcher has a pad layout; there is
  none on this platform, so the page shows as the original without one.
- sg-pc: manual.mpk mount, hud/helpmenu.lua.
- 0023's HELP fallback (raise SF_SUBMENUEXIT at once) now only applies when the profile has no help menu.

Checked on MuMu (Android 15): HELP from the title and from the in-game system menu matches screenshots of the
original (page, page number, tabs, guide), tab tap and E / Q change the page with the slide, Backspace and the
two-finger back return to the title / system menu, reopening starts at page 1.

